{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166127-kingdom-of-atlantis-shard","id":1166127,"title":"Kingdom of Atlantis [Shard]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-08T10:46:47-08:00","id":1166127,"title":"Kingdom of Atlantis [Shard]","content":"(inspired by the Darksword Chronicles)<br /> <br /> Welcome to the magical land of <b>Atlantis</b>.<br /> <br /> Long ago, so long that no written record of the time has survived since that time, the Ancient Ones has left the<b> World of Sleep</b> where magic has died out, and their kind were chased down and killed for being Awake. Using a great magic preformed by the the representatives of the <b>Eleven Awakened Mysteries</b>, the Ancients has gathered whatever little magic which was left in the Sleep and reached out through space and time, fate and spirit, life and death, mind, void and God, and reached to the <b>Heart </b>of all magic. There, using a spell which was never pronounced again and its knowledge was erased from reality itself, the Eleven has shattered the Heart from the world, creating for themselves an haven where magic could roam free, unbound by the Sleep of Reason and the threat it posed upon the world- locking it outside of the world, beyond the <b>Abyss</b>. There, magic and its practitioners could finally bloom, creating wonders- and horrors- which no mortal mind could ever imagine. All that was left for them to do was to give that magical world a name- and so they did. They named it Atlantis.<br /> <br /> That was Atlantis's Golden Age- the practitioners of the Eleven Mysteries has lived together as a part of the <b>Dragon Empire</b>. <b>Five Watchtowers</b> were established in Atlantis, to gather the magic from the Heart and spread it through the realm. The <b>Six Orders</b> then were established to rule the Empire and supervise the use of magic into perfect, wondrous harmony- the <b>Claw of the Dragon</b> to fight against the ancient horrors which lurked in the new world and never accepted the presence of the newcomers in their world, the<b> Eye of the Dragon</b> to watch the citizens and make sure none shall break the laws or use magic in a way which would endanger the Empire, the <b>Voice of the Dragon</b> to make the said laws and speak for the people, the <b>Wing of the Dragon</b> to collect and research new magical phenomena and spells, the <b>Scales of the Dragon</b> to manage the Church of Awakening and the bureaucracy of magic and the <b>Blood of the Dragon</b> to rule above all. Each person in the Empire was destined from birth to a certain task, which they'll fulfill as adults depending on the Mystery to which they were born- <b>Warlocks </b>to the Mystery of Mind, <b>Conjurers </b>for Space, <b>Witches </b>for Fate, <b>Diviners </b>for Time, <b>Alchemists </b>for Matter, <b>Necromancers </b>for Death, <b>Shamans </b>for Spirit, <b>Druids </b>for Life, <b>Evokers </b>for Force, <b>Theurges </b>for Prime and <b>Sorcerers</b> for Sleep. For centuries, the system worked well, and the age of wonders and peace has spread through Atlantis.<br /> <br /> Yet, no sun shines forever, and even the gold lose its luster. Through the kingdom, dissent has started to rise, especially among the lower caste members. People has started to rebel against the system, claiming that it was corrupted and didn't allow equal place for all members of society. First among them were the Sorcerers, for they claimed that they Mystery was frowned upon and treated unfairly. While the Eye has done its best to qualm the mayhem, its actions has only enhance the flames, for the rebels has saw how their leaders have vanished in the middle of the night without trace. Eventually, an all out rebellion against the Empire, leading the many warring faction into a single body called the <b>Nameless</b>. While each of the Nameless factions has their own opinion about how to deal with the situation, three main sects were the most powerful- the <b>Free Council</b>, made out mostly from farmers and lower caste members who wished for an equal status, the <b>Obelisk of Sleep</b>, which was made mostly from Sorcerers, and the <b>Fearful Ones</b>, which believed that the Empire is squeezing the Heart too much and by doing so endanger bringing the death of magic- something which condemned them as heretics in the eyes of the Church.<br /> <br /> As the rebellions grew, the Empire faced the fact they only had two choices before them- to send the Claw against their own citizens, or turn to negotiation. Setting for a meeting between the representatives of both the Dragon Empire and the Nameless, the Empire was willing to grant certain rights for the rebels- such as loosing a bit the caste system, or given some more freedom for voicing different opinions against the Empire's will. The Council tended to accept the agreement, but the two other factions had plans of their own. In the middle of one such meetings, by using foul magic developed from the depths of Sleep, they attacked the Imperial Palace, killing most of the members of the Blood and then launched an attack against the Watchtowers to destroy the monopoly of the Empire over magic once and for all.<br /> <br /> That even has triggered the<b> Nameless Wars</b>. It was a bloody time, where one mage has turned against the other, using magic to bring destruction instead of creation. Only through great sacrifices the Watchtowers were saved, and many horrors were conjured or unleashed in order to fight the agents of the dark arts. Much of Atlantis's glory has faded away during those dark times, but eventually the Empire has won- and lost. The Obelisk and the Fearful were shattered and killed, together with many of the innocent Councilors, but the price was great. The Blood of the Dragon was destroyed, with the only exception of ten members. The Orders were mostly shattered, and the Empire could no longer maintain a unified rule through Atlantis. The Claw has discovered they lost control over the horrors they summoned, leaving them to roam free through the land and butcher any poor soul which stumbled upon their way. Many great wonders of the past were gone, and the magical knowledge was forever lost. The Empire has died, and not even the greatest of necromancers could have bring it back from the grave.<br /> <br /> That was when the Scales came up with a suggestion- instead of a unified Empire, Atlantis would be divided into ten different city states, each ruled by the lineage of one of the surviving members of the Blood. The Orders would reform, but would act more or less independently and serve their own cities first and foremost, even though they will serve as the connecting link. Each of the five orders would base itself in one of the Watchtowers, while the the Scales would maintain presence over the Heart, so they'll guarantee that magic would be safe and protected. The Mystery of Sleep was outlawed, and anyone who were to be found practicing it, or breaking the laws by destroying magic or starting a rebellion or by posing any threat for the existence of magic and stability of Atlantis would be thrown into the Abyss, back to Sleep. While the Orders didn't liked giving the Scales the power over the Heart of Magic, they were tired from war and the Scales were the largest, most powerful Order for it was one with the Church, giving them the support of the masses. And so, they agreed.<br /> <br /> That has led to a new age of Atlantis- one which was not as beautiful, but was the best one could have achieved. The Dragon Orders were no more, and the ten cities were established from the Empire's ruins, each of them being ruled by one of the royal <b>Exarchs</b>. The cities were <b>Aether</b>, the sacred city ruled by the<b> Father of Heavens</b>, <b>Arcadia</b>, the garden of storytellers ruled by the <b>Princess of Ruin</b>, <b>Kigal</b>, the silent necropolis ruled by the <b>Guardian of Paths</b>, <b>Tengri</b>, the dark city ruled by the <b>Nemesis of Shadows</b>, <b>Pandemonium</b>, the great labyrinth ruled by the <b>Watching Eye</b>, <b>Stygia</b>, the city of gold ruled by the <b>Chancellor of Souls</b>, <b>Yggdrasil</b>, the forest haven ruled by the <b>Queen of Raptors</b>, <b>Qaf</b>, which is resides in the burning sands and is ruled by the<b> General of Storms</b>, <b>Duat</b>, the city of broken pillars ruled by the <b>Silent Prophet</b> and <b>Naraka</b>, the peaceful city which is ruled by the <b>Unifying Tyrant</b>. The six Orders which bind those disparate city states together are the <b>Seers of the Throne</b>, the priesthood and advisers of the Exarchs which rose from the Scales and reside in the Heart of Magic and the <b>Watchtower of Silver Thorn</b>, the <b>Silver Ladder</b>, the judges of Atlantis which rose from the Voice and reside in the <b>Watchtower of Golden Key</b>, the <b>Adamantine Arrow,</b> the armies of each of the city states which rose from the Claw and reside in the <b>Watchtower of the Singing Stone</b>, the <b>Guardians of the Veil,</b> the secret police that works behind the scenes which rose from the Eye and reside in the <b>Watchtower of Iron Gauntlet</b> and the <b>Mysterium</b>, that search for the lost wonders of the fallen golden age which rose from the Wing and reside in the <b>Watchtower of Lead Coin</b>. Outside of the lands controlled by the city states and the Watchtowers were the<b> Nameless Lands</b>, to which the surviving renegades of the losing side have escaped to lick their wounds, surrounded by magic which got out of control and monsters created and summoned by magic. The Free Council has became the only unifying power in those lands, accepting to its ranks outlaws, rebels and wanted individuals who wished for a sanctuary from the Orders, as the other two factions who shattered beyond repair.<br /> <br /> At least, that's what they thought.<br /> <br /> That system has lasted for years, as the five <b>Oracles </b>of each of the Orders maintain regulation over magic and the Exarchs maintained the peace from one generation to the other. Wars have broke from time to time, but by using magical powers and following protocols handed by the Orders almost no blood has been spilled on Atlantis. As the Sorcerers were killed or escaped the Nameless Lands, no new children to the Mystery of Sleep were born, and those who were caught practicing the art at later ages were immediately thrown to the Abyss. Slowly, the fear from the Eleventh Mystery was forgotten- for there was no Sleeping child in the land of the Awakened.<br /> <br /> Until the day that the Aether's Father and Mother gave birth to a Sleeping Child.<br /> <br /> The child wasn't just born to the Mystery of Sleep- he was a <b>Sleeper</b>. Not even a spark of magic burn inside of him, and his very existence was a threat to Atlantis's existence. The Oracle of Silver Thorn has pronounced the child as dead and took him to the heart, never to be seen again- and leaving Aether without a child. After that, more children were suddenly born to the Mystery of Sleep for the nobles of the different city states, leaving the citizens of Atlantis in panic. More then one time the parents has tried to hide their children from the Church, forcing the Guardians of the Veil to spy after the parents and steal children from their cribs. The Seers preached against the act and worked to consul the grieving parents, and the Ladder worked hard to convince the masses of the necessity of the act, all that while Mysterium searched to books for a way to stop the phenomena without success. However, some parents have managed to escape with their children to the Nameless Lands, where they grew their children among the outlaws. Few years later, reports has started to come to the Arrow that the Sorcerers has started to organize once more in the Nameless Lands, reestablishing the Obelisk. From the other, the shattered remains of the Fearful Ones has started to smell the weakness in the magic, and their ideology became almost infectious in the Nameless Lands, creating the same faction under a different name- the <b>Eaters of Fear</b>. The Guardians, on the other hand, got reports on a new, terrorist group which has hid in the Nameless Lands for centuries bat lately is has started to crawl its way into the Awakened Lands- the <b>Hollow Palace</b>, soul thieves which claim themselves as the true heirs of the Blood and followers of their own Exarch called the the Keeper of Gates. The rise of the new threats has caused the the Council to loose power and influence, forcing it to work once more with its enemies for the fear they would turn upon them, yet unable to ask for help from the Orders. With that lose of control, the <b>Apostate Cults of the Fallen</b> has started to rise- a collection of mages who practice the foulest of magics, gaining power from the horrors and wild magic which were unleashed during the Nameless Wars. The Bound, the original inhabitants of Atlantis, start to break free from their bindings, gathering faithful to their service under the name of the <b>Covens of Dusk</b>. The monsters of the Nameless Lands become restless, and attacks against humans becomes more and more common.<br /> <br /> The common citizen doesn't know anything of that, of course. The Oracles promise them that magic keeps functioning undisturbed and that the best of their people work on trying to put an end to the Mystery. The Exarchs preform one celebration after the other, telling their people that they are safe and silencing any rumors about what that happens in the Nameless Lands. The Sorcerers are long forgotten threat, they promise. The Nameless Lands are full only of monsters, and even they can't deal with the power of the Arrow. Atlantis is as strong as ever, and everyone who dares to speak others is quickly silenced. Atlantis is perfect- everyone agrees with that. Saying otherwise is heresy, and there is only one punishment worthy for heretics- being thrown to the Abyss. And so, everyone keep on smiling, keep on celebrating and keep on living as if nothing has changed- but the fear keep on boiling deep down in their heart. And that practice, that pretendence, ended up being given a name- that is, the <b>Lie</b>.<br /> <br /> Atlantis is found on the edge. It would take nothing more than a single push to destroy it- or to save it, and no one knows to which direction the push is needed in order to do what, and as such they prefer to do nothing. But the Lie can't survive forever- someday, somehow, all hell would break loose- and who knows? Perhaps the Awakened would discover that they were the ones asleep all along, and that it is the time to awake from their beautiful dream...<br /> <br /> Welcome to the magical land of Atlantis.<br /> <br /> Enjoy it while it lasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 12-08-2017, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T10:52:59-08:00","id":1166129,"title":"","content":"so, here is my basic idea for an alternative setting based around the Darksword Chronicles. That's the general outline of the setting, and I'll start with the needed mechanical modifications in future posts. Tell me if there is something you are extremely excited to see (such as Mysteries /Orders /Exarchates /Watchtowers /Nameless /Monsters /etc) so I'll know what to write first!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}